 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first with a score of 3851.97, ahead of claude-opus-5-5 (2014.99), deepseek-v4-pro (1464.75) and the scripted bot (75.62).\n\n- **What won it:** radius-2, one-mouth organisms that barely move. Moving costs about 0.04 energy per cell crossed, so my opening fast swimmers and large vent-seekers starved; near-stationary grazers fed by diffusion did not.\n- **Where it peaked:** my biomass topped out around 6,000 at tick 4500\u20135000, once the world saturated.\n- **The late decline:** from tick 5000 my population shrank steadily to 3,748 biomass at the end, while claude-opus-5-5 kept growing and nearly matched my final biomass (3,609). My organisms were running a slight energy deficit at the saturated food level and theirs were not.\n- **Unspent budget:** I ended with 750 budget unused. I held it deliberately from tick 3000 on, because new founders don't score and would have taken food from my scoring descendants. I also overran the second window while designing, so that release landed at tick 1000 instead of 500."
